    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "image",
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "claude-opus-4-7",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "claude-opus-4-7"
        },
        "text": "=You are an OMR scanner.\n\nYou MUST decide based on darkness threshold.\n\nFor each row:\n1. Compare all 4 bubbles.\n2. A bubble is VALID only if it is SIGNIFICANTLY darker than the others.\n\nCRITICAL RULE:\n- If no bubble is clearly darker than the rest → return null\n- If all bubbles look similar → return null\n- If shading is uniform or faint → return null\n- NEVER guess\n\nSTRICT:\n- Prefer null over guessing\n- If unsure → null\n\nDO NOT:\n- infer patterns\n- assume an answer exists\n- try to distribute answers evenly\n\nEach row is independent.\n\nOutput:\n- 1 = leftmost\n- 2 = second\n- 3 = third\n- 4 = rightmost\n- null = no clear mark\n\nReturn ONLY JSON:\n{\"answers\":[...]}",
        "inputType": "binary",
        "binaryPropertyName": "=block_file",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.anthropic",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2368,
        48
      ],
      "id": "6afa9080-71e5-4b4a-baad-bbc163aa2933",
      "name": "Analyze image",
      "credentials": {
        "anthropicApi": {
          "id": "e1ZvH7vjvR4qwrjt",
          "name": "Anthropic account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "return [{\n  json: {\n    ...$json,\n    _binary_backup: $binary   // store it safely\n  },\n  binary: $binary\n}];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2160,
        48
      ],
      "id": "9944779b-cfbf-4722-9408-533c099beff7",
      "name": "Preserve Binary"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const items = $input.all();\n\nfunction initArray(size) {\n  return Array(size).fill(null);\n}\n\n// exact section sizes\nlet result = {\n  english: initArray(50),\n  math: initArray(45),\n  reading: initArray(36),\n  science: initArray(40)\n};\n\nitems.forEach((item, index) => {\n  const answers = item.json.answers;\n  if (!answers) return;\n\n  let section, start;\n\n  // ENGLISH (runs 0–4)\n  if (index < 5) {\n    section = \"english\";\n    start = index * 10;\n  }\n\n  // MATH (runs 5–9)\n  else if (index < 10) {\n    section = \"math\";\n    const col = index - 5;\n\n    if (col < 4) start = col * 10;\n    else start = 40; // last column (5 questions)\n  }\n\n  // READING (runs 10–14)\n  else if (index < 15) {\n    section = \"reading\";\n    const col = index - 10;\n\n    if (col < 4) start = col * 8;\n    else start = 32;\n  }\n\n  // SCIENCE (runs 15–19)\n  else if (index < 20) {\n    section = \"science\";\n    const col = index - 15;\n\n    start = col * 8;\n  }\n\n  // place answers safely\n  answers.forEach((ans, i) => {\n    const pos = start + i;\n\n    if (pos < result[section].length) {\n      result[section][pos] = ans;\n    }\n  });\n});\n\nreturn [{\n  json: result\n}];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2224,
        -128
      ],
      "id": "68d9113e-20ca-495a-af85-03a72c09ad66",
      "name": "Code in JavaScript"
